A listing's field mapping types a site's own catalog column by its field on the site's content types: the field of the same name on the edited page's type, else on the site's other types, so a list column (a `KeywordIndex`-style field) maps onto a list. Before, every such column was text, and a list column mapped onto tags was refused. A column no type has a field for stays text; one whose types hold it differently isn't offered. The save check, the mapping widget and `plone-content` (`--content-types <types.json>`) read the same rule; checking such a listing offline now needs the content types. #728
